#18203
The Temple Common Area~
   This is a large room with a vaulted ceiling, kept clean and spartan by
the monks that live here. All is quiet now, except for the light sound of
bare feet walking across the spotless white marble floor, and the rhythmic
chanting coming from the room to the west.
   The view from this open hillside building is absolutely splendid. You can
see the city of Kir-Oshi in all its wonder to the east. In the distance to
the north, you can see the vast, rolling plains of dor-Sefrith; even further
is the silhouette of the Grey Mountains.
   The entrance to the temple is to the east, the altar to the north. To
the south, ordinary citizens have left offerings for the less fortunate.
~
