stub of candle placed unceremoniously in the northwestern corner. Entrails
have been heaped in small piles in various parts of the room, glistening
like swollen fruit. Dried pools of blood, now almost black, have been
splattered on the walls. The putrid smell of decay gives you a nauseating
feeling in the pit of your stomach. The only exit is the stairs from which
you came.
