runes~
0~
The runes are magical in nature, emanating a faint luminescence even when it
is bright daylight in the open harbor. They have been etched into the wood of
the pier meticiously, and they look as if they are used to summon something,
but what you can only speculate. The passersby of the pier go out of their
way to avoid walking on it, their superstitious nature bringing fear of the
perternatural malevolence assosicated with the runes. In the middle of them
there is a phrase, and although you don't understand the symbols, their
meaning is somehow clear in your mind:

"That is not dead which can eternal lie,
And with strange aeons even death may die."
~
