   The icy sea-water surrounding you chills you to the very marrow, as you
fight to move yourself along. If you're exposed to this for much longer,
you might succumb to hypothermia. What a terrible end that would be.
   The passage continues to the east and west, though in the darkness of
this water-filled cavern, it is incredibly difficult to tell which direction
to go to reach dry land.
~
